WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.301
Module 2: the Mosaic ecosystem.

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:04.527
Clients rarely ask for a tool.

00:00:04.527 --> 00:00:06.011
They ask a question.

00:00:06.011 --> 00:00:08.312
What's our culture really like?

00:00:08.312 --> 00:00:09.573
Is our COO ready?

00:00:09.573 --> 00:00:12.393
Did anything we did make a difference?

00:00:12.393 --> 00:00:18.330
Your job is to hear the question and pick
the tool, or the combination of tools,

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.518
that answers it.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:22.857
This module takes about
seventy-five minutes.

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:26.040
Each tool answers a different question.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.672
The Culture Mosaic answers:
what is our culture like?

00:00:29.672 --> 00:00:35.429
The Culture Progress Monitor answers: has
it changed where we've been working on it?

00:00:35.429 --> 00:00:39.884
The Leadership Mosaic 360 answers:
how is this leader showing up,

00:00:39.884 --> 00:00:41.666
as they and others see it?

00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:45.572
And its Team Report does the
same for a group of leaders.

00:00:45.572 --> 00:00:49.616
Mosaic Signal answers: what
stories sit behind the numbers?

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:55.236
And Culture Dig answers: why is our culture
this way, and what is it really doing?

00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:58.377
Let's look at each tool more closely.

00:00:58.377 --> 00:01:02.593
The Culture Mosaic looks at
the organization, or a subteam.

00:01:02.593 --> 00:01:07.809
It's an anonymous survey of fifty-four
statements on a one-to-five scale,

00:01:07.809 --> 00:01:11.668
about ten minutes per person,
with two open questions.

00:01:11.668 --> 00:01:16.599
It also produces a Psychological
Safety Index from four of the items.

00:01:16.599 --> 00:01:21.315
You can add subscales, your own
questions, demographic breakdowns,

00:01:21.315 --> 00:01:23.101
and an executive readout.

00:01:23.101 --> 00:01:27.817
It produces a designed PowerPoint
report built around the diamond.

00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:33.248
The Culture Progress Monitor re-measures
one to three of the twelve domains.

00:01:33.248 --> 00:01:36.821
It's built as a copy of an
earlier Culture Mosaic,

00:01:36.821 --> 00:01:42.680
which must have run in SurveyCraft in the
same organization and have at least five

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.109
completed responses.

00:01:44.109 --> 00:01:47.110
Its report shows each domain then and now,

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:50.254
and labels each change
as meaningful or not.

00:01:50.254 --> 00:01:55.542
The Leadership Mosaic 360 looks at one
leader: fifty-seven statements on a

00:01:55.542 --> 00:01:58.829
one-to-seven scale, plus
three open questions.

00:01:58.829 --> 00:02:02.474
The leader rates themselves,
and their boss, peers,

00:02:02.474 --> 00:02:07.404
direct reports and others rate them,
in any of twenty-nine languages.

00:02:07.404 --> 00:02:11.263
The Team Report combines
three to twenty-five leaders.

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:16.550
Mosaic Signal asks people to tell a
short story from their own experience,

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:20.766
then interpret their own story
with a few visual questions.

00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:25.125
It produces interactive charts
that link back to the stories.

00:02:25.125 --> 00:02:28.126
There's no scored report and no benchmark.

00:02:28.126 --> 00:02:34.129
And Culture Dig is an eight to twelve week
research program built on Schein's model.

00:02:34.129 --> 00:02:38.273
Seven small research teams
study seven domains of culture,

00:02:38.273 --> 00:02:41.703
while everyone else
contributes one short story.

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:46.634
It produces a findings report, and
it can repeat in up to four waves.

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:49.420
Buying it online gets you the software.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.493
Facilitation by the Mosaic
team is a separate engagement.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.346
Start with whose behaviour
the question is about,

00:02:57.346 --> 00:03:00.215
then what kind of answer the client needs.

00:03:00.215 --> 00:03:05.610
If it's about one leader, or a group of
leaders, use the Leadership Mosaic 360,

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:11.073
and add the Team Report when three or more
leaders on one team have closed 360s.

00:03:11.073 --> 00:03:15.581
If it's about the organization,
ask what kind of answer they need.

00:03:15.581 --> 00:03:19.200
A broad picture, comparable
with other organizations?

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.976
That's the Culture Mosaic.

00:03:20.976 --> 00:03:22.000
Has it changed?

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.912
That's the Progress Monitor.

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:27.532
What's really happening, in
people's own words, fast?

00:03:27.532 --> 00:03:28.488
Mosaic Signal.

00:03:28.488 --> 00:03:32.722
And why is it like this, in depth,
over eight to twelve weeks?

00:03:32.722 --> 00:03:33.542
Culture Dig.

00:03:33.542 --> 00:03:36.615
Then check the constraints
before you commit.

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:39.688
Are there enough people
to protect anonymity?

00:03:39.688 --> 00:03:43.513
Is there a prior Culture Mosaic
if this is a re-measure?

00:03:43.513 --> 00:03:46.449
Is there time and people
for a Culture Dig?

00:03:46.449 --> 00:03:50.137
And can it launch within
about two months of purchase?

00:03:50.633 --> 00:03:51.594
Let's practise.

00:03:51.594 --> 00:03:54.540
You'll see six client
requests, one at a time.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:59.855
For each one, pick the best first tool,
then read why the others don't fit as well.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.829
Every Mosaic tool works on its own.

00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:06.910
A client can run just a Mosaic
Signal, just a Culture Dig,

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:12.750
or just a Leadership Mosaic 360, and get
a complete answer to the question it asks.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.619
The tools are also designed
to work together over time.

00:04:16.619 --> 00:04:20.841
Mosaic Signal and Culture Dig
in particular can stand alone,

00:04:20.841 --> 00:04:25.274
or supplement a larger culture
study built on a Culture Mosaic.

00:04:25.274 --> 00:04:30.410
When a client wants the full picture,
an engagement often runs like this.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.787
Measure the whole culture
with a Culture Mosaic.

00:04:33.787 --> 00:04:38.079
Go deeper where it matters with
Mosaic Signal or Culture Dig,

00:04:38.079 --> 00:04:43.496
and develop the leaders who carry the
culture with the Leadership Mosaic 360.

00:04:43.496 --> 00:04:47.296
Then check progress with the
Culture Progress Monitor.

00:04:47.296 --> 00:04:49.477
That rhythm is ADDIS in action.

00:04:49.967 --> 00:04:53.592
Here are four patterns
Mosaic practitioners use.

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:56.840
Treat them as starting
points, not recipes.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.333
Any tool can also run on its own.

00:04:59.333 --> 00:05:01.523
One: diagnose, deepen, track.

00:05:01.523 --> 00:05:07.717
A Culture Mosaic, then Mosaic Signal or
Culture Dig on the lowest or most puzzling

00:05:07.717 --> 00:05:13.835
tiles, then a Progress Monitor on one to
three domains about six to twelve months

00:05:13.835 --> 00:05:14.288
later.

00:05:14.288 --> 00:05:16.857
Good for most culture engagements.

00:05:16.857 --> 00:05:19.198
Two: leaders alongside culture.

00:05:19.198 --> 00:05:22.068
A Culture Mosaic for the organization,

00:05:22.068 --> 00:05:27.733
plus a 360 for each member of the top
team and a Team Report for the group.

00:05:27.733 --> 00:05:33.247
Good when the culture's weak spots
may reflect how the senior team leads,

00:05:33.247 --> 00:05:36.948
and present that as a
hypothesis, never as proof.

00:05:36.948 --> 00:05:42.916
Three: a coaching engagement, where a
coach launches a 360 from Mosaic Coaching

00:05:42.916 --> 00:05:43.444
Studio.

00:05:43.444 --> 00:05:45.710
And four: a change initiative,

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:51.526
where a Mosaic Signal Change Readiness
Assessment runs before or early in the

00:05:51.526 --> 00:05:54.019
change, and you re-measure later.

00:05:54.533 --> 00:05:57.448
Here's the path Northwind Health took.

00:05:57.448 --> 00:06:03.583
In February and March 2026, a Culture
Mosaic census of all six hundred and forty

00:06:03.583 --> 00:06:04.350
employees.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:08.108
Then a Mosaic Signal Change
Readiness Assessment,

00:06:08.108 --> 00:06:11.866
collecting stories from
nursing and clinic staff.

00:06:11.866 --> 00:06:18.232
Then 360s for all six executives, and in
June a Team Report for the executive team.

00:06:18.232 --> 00:06:24.137
From April to September they worked on
the three lowest tiles: Collaboration,

00:06:24.137 --> 00:06:26.668
Change Ready and Empowered Teams.

00:06:26.668 --> 00:06:30.886
In October, a Progress Monitor
re-measured those three.

00:06:30.886 --> 00:06:37.021
Before you continue, think about this:
why did Northwind run Mosaic Signal after

00:06:37.021 --> 00:06:40.013
the Culture Mosaic, rather than before?

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:45.385
Every Mosaic tool is built so that
nobody's answers can be picked out.

00:06:45.385 --> 00:06:47.897
The product enforces these minimums.

00:06:47.897 --> 00:06:52.015
Your job is to plan around
them, never to work around them.

00:06:52.015 --> 00:06:56.132
A whole-organization report
needs five completed responses.

00:06:56.132 --> 00:06:59.133
A report filtered to
one subteam needs ten.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:02.622
Demographic groups smaller
than three, by default,

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:04.995
are merged into "Other" or hidden.

00:07:04.995 --> 00:07:10.438
In a 360, peers, direct reports and others
each need three completed raters to

00:07:10.438 --> 00:07:11.834
appear on their own.

00:07:11.834 --> 00:07:16.579
Smaller groups are folded together,
and their comments are withheld.

00:07:16.579 --> 00:07:18.463
Boss feedback is different.

00:07:18.463 --> 00:07:22.999
In an individual 360 report, bosses
are named, up to two of them.

00:07:22.999 --> 00:07:25.163
Tell raters this before launch.

00:07:25.163 --> 00:07:28.931
In the Team Report, bosses
are pooled and never named.

00:07:28.931 --> 00:07:31.792
Culture surveys are anonymous by default.

00:07:31.792 --> 00:07:35.561
A roster tracks who has
completed, not what they said.

00:07:35.561 --> 00:07:40.027
And test responses never count
toward a report or the benchmark.

00:07:40.027 --> 00:07:42.609
In practice, when you scope a survey,

00:07:42.609 --> 00:07:46.308
count the smallest group
the client will want to see.

00:07:46.308 --> 00:07:50.774
If a department has six people,
they won't get a subteam report,

00:07:50.774 --> 00:07:52.938
and you should say so up front.

00:07:53.433 --> 00:07:57.657
The Mosaic benchmark makes
percentile comparisons possible.

00:07:57.657 --> 00:07:59.303
Joining is the default.

00:07:59.303 --> 00:08:04.028
A Culture Mosaic adds its organization,
and a 360 adds its leader,

00:08:04.028 --> 00:08:08.108
when the report is generated
after the survey has closed.

00:08:08.108 --> 00:08:11.401
What's added is de-identified,
aggregate data.

00:08:11.401 --> 00:08:13.763
Several things keep a survey out.

00:08:13.763 --> 00:08:18.488
The owner can turn off the benchmark
switch on the responses page,

00:08:18.488 --> 00:08:22.067
and turning it off later
withdraws what was added.

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:26.505
The buyer may have declined the
research database at checkout.

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:32.446
A report generated before close doesn't
join, nor does a subteam report, test data,

00:08:32.446 --> 00:08:36.169
or a Culture Mosaic with
fewer than ten respondents.

00:08:36.169 --> 00:08:40.822
And two tools never join: the
Progress Monitor and Mosaic Signal.

00:08:40.822 --> 00:08:44.472
If a client asks to stay
out, show them the switch.

00:08:44.472 --> 00:08:48.839
It's their choice, and they lose
nothing in their own report.

00:08:49.333 --> 00:08:50.597
Three more rules.

00:08:50.597 --> 00:08:53.422
First, launch within about two months.

00:08:53.422 --> 00:08:59.369
A purchased Culture Mosaic, Progress
Monitor or Mosaic Signal must launch within

00:08:59.369 --> 00:09:05.018
about two months of purchase, so plan
the client's timeline before they buy.

00:09:05.018 --> 00:09:07.471
Second, one purchase, one launch.

00:09:07.471 --> 00:09:11.336
A bought survey can't be
duplicated into a free one.

00:09:11.336 --> 00:09:16.540
To run it again, buy another, or for
a re-measure, a Progress Monitor.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:22.635
Purchased respondent limits can be lowered,
but never raised past what was bought.

00:09:22.635 --> 00:09:25.014
Third, locked items stay locked.

00:09:25.014 --> 00:09:29.771
The standard statements can't be
reworded, reordered or deleted,

00:09:29.771 --> 00:09:33.934
because that would break
comparisons with the benchmark.

00:09:33.934 --> 00:09:38.543
And in SurveyCraft, roles run
from Owner, to Admin, to Editor,

00:09:38.543 --> 00:09:43.746
who builds surveys and generates
reports, to Viewer, who sees results.

00:09:44.233 --> 00:09:48.340
If you're a Mosaic partner, here's
how the commercial side works.

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:51.183
Your partner code works
on every Mosaic tool.

00:09:51.183 --> 00:09:53.457
It's a discount applied at checkout,

00:09:53.457 --> 00:09:57.563
and what it's worth depends on
your badges in the partner portal.

00:09:57.563 --> 00:10:00.027
Only one discount applies per checkout.

00:10:00.027 --> 00:10:02.364
And it's for your own purchases only.

00:10:02.364 --> 00:10:05.018
You must be signed in with your own email.

00:10:05.018 --> 00:10:09.693
When something bought with your code
closes with at least three responses,

00:10:09.693 --> 00:10:13.673
it counts as a launch, and launches
build your tool-use badges.

00:10:13.673 --> 00:10:16.895
When your profile is complete
you earn Profile Pro,

00:10:16.895 --> 00:10:22.012
which gives you one free run: a Culture
Mosaic for up to twenty-five respondents,

00:10:22.012 --> 00:10:24.160
or one Leadership Mosaic 360 seat.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:28.835
Coaches can also launch Mosaic tools
straight from Mosaic Coaching Studio.

00:10:28.835 --> 00:10:32.309
Prices aren't part of this
course, because they change.

00:10:32.309 --> 00:10:35.721
Check the current Mosaic
price sheet before you quote.

00:10:36.233 --> 00:10:36.986
One warning.

00:10:36.986 --> 00:10:41.128
Don't give your partner code to a
client to use at their checkout.

00:10:41.128 --> 00:10:45.082
It will be refused, and sharing
it breaks the Code of Practice.

00:10:45.082 --> 00:10:48.659
If a client should buy directly,
they pay the list price,

00:10:48.659 --> 00:10:51.985
or they talk to the Mosaic
team about the engagement.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:58.349
Here's your Tool Selector: one column per
tool, with what it answers, its level,

00:10:58.349 --> 00:11:03.613
data, time, output, benchmark rules,
and the one thing to watch out for.

00:11:03.613 --> 00:11:04.490
Download it.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:10.278
And here's the Confidentiality Thresholds
card, with every minimum in one place.

00:11:10.278 --> 00:11:12.784
Keep it handy when you scope a client.

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:13.997
To recap.

00:11:13.997 --> 00:11:16.941
Hear the question, then pick the tool.

00:11:16.941 --> 00:11:23.060
Each tool stands alone, and Mosaic Signal
and Culture Dig can also supplement a

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.687
Culture Mosaic study.

00:11:24.687 --> 00:11:31.038
The thresholds protect people: five for an
organization report, ten for a subteam,

00:11:31.038 --> 00:11:35.376
a minimum group of three,
three raters per 360 category,

00:11:35.376 --> 00:11:38.474
and bosses are named in individual 360s.

00:11:38.474 --> 00:11:43.664
The benchmark joins by default
after close, the client can opt out,

00:11:43.664 --> 00:11:47.847
and the Progress Monitor and
Mosaic Signal never join.

00:11:47.847 --> 00:11:52.185
Launch within about two months,
one purchase per launch.

00:11:52.185 --> 00:11:55.051
And your partner code is yours alone.

00:11:55.051 --> 00:11:57.297
Next, choose any tool module.

00:11:57.297 --> 00:12:02.332
If your next engagement is a
culture survey, start with Module 3.

